WEBVTT

NOTE MedX walkthrough, narrated. Synthetic data only. Generated by scripts/record-demo.mjs.

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.420 line:84.1% align:center
This is MedX.

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.920 line:84.1% align:center
When patients and staff don’t share a language,

3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.100 line:84.1% align:center
an allergy can get lost.

4
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.290 line:84.1% align:center
So before the visit, patients tell Fin what’s wrong,

5
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.110 line:84.1% align:center
in English, Thai or Italian.

6
00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.450 line:84.1% align:center
This synthetic patient has a penicillin allergy,

7
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.490 line:84.1% align:center
and checks every word.

8
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.620 line:84.1% align:center
They get a visit code.

9
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.860 line:84.1% align:center
MedX drafts a short summary from their words,

10
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.240 line:84.1% align:center
and a nurse reviews it before anything is final.

11
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.230 line:84.1% align:center
The visit lands in the nurse’s review queue.

12
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.140 line:51.5% align:center
The nurse signs in by name; every change is recorded.

13
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:36.090 line:84.1% align:center
Every drafted field links to the patient’s own words,

14
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.190 line:84.1% align:center
and a program checks each quote is really there.

15
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.050 line:84.1% align:center
Then the nurse approves.

16
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.640 line:84.1% align:center
A Thai patient’s words reach the nurse the same way,

17
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.680 line:84.1% align:center
quote by quote.

18
00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.270 line:84.1% align:center
Back to our patient. The nurse records vitals.

19
00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.390 line:84.1% align:center
NEWS2 suggests a triage level; the nurse confirms.

20
00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.550 line:84.1% align:center
MedX never decides urgency.

21
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.900 line:84.1% align:center
The doctor sees rule-based considerations,

22
00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.860 line:84.1% align:center
each marked “not a diagnosis”, and keeps one.

23
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.170 line:84.1% align:center
The doctor signs the note. Only then is it final.

24
00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.760 line:84.1% align:center
Watch the allergy. The doctor orders amoxicillin, a penicillin.

25
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.020 line:84.1% align:center
A rule check flags it,

26
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.520 line:84.1% align:center
and the doctor asks the pharmacy to review.

27
00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.110 line:74.4% align:center
Pharmacist 1 returns the order with a report,

28
00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.670 line:74.4% align:center
suggesting clarithromycin for prescriber review.

29
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.980 line:84.1% align:center
The doctor changes the order to clarithromycin and resubmits.

30
00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.810 line:74.4% align:center
Pharmacist 1 verifies the corrected prescription.

31
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.100 line:74.4% align:center
One more safety net: whoever verified cannot dispense.

32
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.240 line:74.4% align:center
A second pharmacist signs in.

33
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.030 line:74.4% align:center
Pharmacist 2 ticks six final checks before dispensing.

34
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.100 line:74.4% align:center
Then they call the patient to counter 2.

35
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.590 line:84.1% align:center
The patient’s phone shows ready at counter 2.

36
00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.690 line:84.1% align:center
No drug names, no notes.

37
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.060 line:84.1% align:center
Operations sees each stage as counts only.

38
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.840 line:84.1% align:center
In this demo, a mock model does the drafting.

39
00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.890 line:84.1% align:center
The case trace shows every step:

40
00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:02.030 line:84.1% align:center
red-flag rules before any model call, then each human decision.

41
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.680 line:84.1% align:center
MedX supports clinicians.

42
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.940 line:84.1% align:center
It never diagnoses, prescribes or decides urgency.

43
00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.860 line:84.1% align:center
Research prototype, synthetic data, not a medical device.

44
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.330 line:84.1% align:center
Try the live demo.
